      "writtenOn": "2019-06-13T06:25:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is always-on vpn something that only applies to the \"admin\"/system user? \n\nIf so I would consider it a bug fix if this is reset for user 0, even if it is called for user 10 in the multiuser/headless user0 world. \n\nYou\u0027re right that the second reset call does seem to do the wrong thing.\n\nCould we do something like the below work?\n\n@Override\npublic void factoryReset() {\n  enforceConnectivityInternalPermission();\n  final int userId \u003d UserHandle.getCallingUserId();\n  Binder.withCleanCallingIdentity(() -\u003e factoryResetInternal(userId));\n}\n\nprivate void factoryResetInternal(int origUserId) {\n  ...\n  // Same logic besides using origUserId for turning off vpn\n  ...\n}",
